The sample teardown-inputs.ts and its test read. evidence/ and history/ are real, cut to one launch; export.json is written by hand and is no run of the private render.

evidence/rows.jsonl is the controller-headless/omp line of a prompt-inputs proof's rows.jsonl, byte for byte, and evidence/composition.json is the same run's composition.json with only that launch left in its two launch tables. The run is a stand-in run of 2026-11-27 in an isolated Linux build pod (rows.jsonl written 05:58:06Z), from 1098e27eaf18b355b7a8b883360e10807507d9b8 plus the uncommitted driver that counts the other messages, with that checkout as the subject and ecd967b17a4e527009dab56f459e0f4e76c0bd25 as the base. Every one of its 14 rows has other_messages_bytes. Its proof.log fails only on the reference outcomes of refs-base.json, which that head does not meet; no row depends on them. Its two parts are that commit's packages/daemon/internal/prompts/roles/controller-root.md and go/controller-headless.md, whose bytes and sha256 the row gives. The command, with LEGION_OMP_PATH set:

bash scripts/e2e/prompt-inputs.sh --base ecd967b17a4e --subject <checkout at 1098e27eaf18b355b7a8b883360e10807507d9b8>

history/rows.jsonl is the controller-headless/omp line of the stand-in run base-standin-a12 of 2026-11-26 (rows.jsonl written 11:51:51Z), byte for byte, whose subject and base were both ecd967b17a4e527009dab56f459e0f4e76c0bd25. That driver did not count the other messages, so the row has no other_messages_bytes and its total leaves them out, and its skill list gave the stand-in's line as each skill's description. It is kept as history, and the test holds that no command takes it for a measurement.

Not captured: export.json. The private render has written no export of the schema prompt-render/2 yet. This one is written in that render's export types (Export, PublicRef, Render, LaunchRow, PartRow, Digest and Control, as its source declares them for prompt-render/1), with the schema prompt-render/2 and the `composed` and `memoryFile` digests that the render's plan adds in that version. Its projects are the neutral ACME and BETA, its private checkout is labelled `main` at a neutral commit, and its public branch is the neutral `sample-branch`. Each launch's parts are the row's two parts under their repository path. roleText and assembled are composed by the render's rule from those two files and a one-line neutral deployment text: "Sample shared deployment text.\n", then "\n", then "Sample deployment text of ACME.\n" (or BETA), under the header "# Deployment instructions (<project>)", and BETA's memory text "Sample memory text of BETA.\n". The real before and after exports are fixture F6, captured from the private render's own runs.

The export was first written at ecd967b17a4e527009dab56f459e0f4e76c0bd25. On 2026-11-27 its public commit moved to 1098e27eaf18b355b7a8b883360e10807507d9b8, whose parent is b28a60ca658499ac05bbf0f845d5ebca5659f113, and its parts, roleText and assembled were composed again from that commit's two files by the same rule. roleText is the two parts joined, with the last line break trimmed. The deployment text is the header, a blank line and the composed text, with the last line break trimmed. assembled is roleText, a blank line and the deployment text. That rule gives the digests the export held at ecd967b17a4e527009dab56f459e0f4e76c0bd25 byte for byte.
